# Admin UX controls

Conventions for wp-admin UI in this plugin (tree admin, settings, attribute panels).

## Row-wise editing tables — Actions last

In any **row editor** (attributes, relations, band fields, similar tabular edit UIs):

- Put **Actions** in the **rightmost column** (header label e.g. “Actions”).
- Row actions (trash / add) live only in that column — never between data columns.
- Prefer shared class `wtt-row-edit-table` + `wtt-col-actions` (right-aligned).
- Status columns such as **Inherited** come **before** Actions, not after.

Column order example (Attributes):

`Name → Type → Mult. → Bindung → Default value → Readonly → Hide → Inherited → Actions`

## Remove / delete

- **Always** use a **trash-can icon** as the primary remove/delete control.
- Reuse: `dashicons dashicons-trash` inside `button-link-delete` / `wtt-row-edit-table__trash`.
- Set `title` and `aria-label` to the i18n remove string.
- Do **not** use a plain text “Remove” / “Delete” button as the primary control.

## Boolean settings

- For simple true/false decisions, **always** use a **slide switch** (`.wtt-switch` / `renderSlideSwitch`), not radio pairs or plain checkboxes.
- Match WordPress admin chrome (neutral track, `#2271b1` when on).
- Radios/checkboxes only when the choice is **not** a binary on/off.

## Flags strip (node / set / media / attribute chrome)

- **One** flags renderer: `WTTSettingsRender.renderFlagsStrip` / `renderFlagsRow` (tree-admin: `renderFlagsStrip` / `renderNodeFlagsRow`).
- Layout: **5 flags per row**, then wrap (`--wtt-flags-cols`, class `.wtt-settings-flags`).
- Each flag = slide switch + label text — **never** checkboxes in a flags strip.
- Prefer plain `{ label, checked, disabled, title, onChange }` descriptors; do not invent a second flags UI per panel.
- Foundation for further node-config unification: `WTTSettingsRender.renderFormRow`.

## Default value (Festwert meta) / node pickers

- UI label **Default value**; own-attr SoT = Relation edge field `default` (OQ-W4 / Q106; own read edge-only ≈ 0.0.431); host `_wtt_attribute_fixed_values` = **inherited** name overrides only. Node Settings use the same label for `_wtt_fixed_*` seeds (**Q115**) — **grayed on builtin Simple** catalog leaves; editable on specializations / typed fields.
- **Read-only** (not Fixed): slide switch in Attributes + Settings; **grayed** in Settings when the node is not an attribute slot (**Q115** / OQ-A3).
- Scalar defaults use value entry; catalog defaults pick under the attribute’s type tree.
- **CatalogChoice** (typed specialization under a type host — Q90; e.g. Währung → Euro/Dollar): max depth of the type’s choice subtree — **depth ≤ 1** → flat `<select>` / simple leaf list; **depth ≥ 2** → shared **node tree picker**. Default/Festwert seeds the selected value when present. Not catalog `enum`. Not automatic for every picker (deep taxonomy / model-binding may still prefer tree).
- Multiplicity: `0..*` / `1..*` → multi-select for Default; required many (`1..*`) → **swap only** (no clear all / no delete last). **Mult `1`:** no empty/`—` in Default ListChooser (must pick a real value; swap only). **Mult `0..1` / `0..*`:** empty/`—` **required** so Default can stay unset (Q116).
- **Sole required list-select (Q116):** If the control **must** have a value (no zero-lower Mult) and there is **exactly one** real option → auto-select and **gray/disable**. Several options → leave selectable. Optional Mult stays open even with one choice and **must include a clear/empty option** (`—` / tooltip “No prefix” where relevant). Same law for Praefix / Unit prefix selects (Mult drives empty — not “Praefix always empty”). No sample fill for optional empty-capable Praefix. Applies to Preferred, CatalogChoice, Default, Binding, and other ListChooser/`<select>` surfaces.

## Do / don’t

- **Default value** (node Settings): **Label → slide switch → field**. Field always visible; switch off → field grayed/disabled (not hidden). No radio pair for on/off.
- **Do** keep Inherited / status columns read-only; Hide uses a slide switch (**default off**).
- **Do** confirm destructive trash actions when deleting persisted data.
- **Don’t** invent a second toggle style per panel; reuse `.wtt-switch`.
- **Don’t** put Actions anywhere except the last column in row editors.
